# Template drift allowlist for zudo-design-token-lint (doc site).
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences so `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Re-authored from scratch for the new thin-preset model (create-zudo-doc
# 2.5.1) during Wave 3 (S5) integration confirm — see issue #116. Note: the
# drift check (scripts/check-template-drift.sh) only walks
# node_modules/create-zudo-doc/templates/{base,features}; top-level identity
# files (zfb.config.ts, wrangler.toml, src/config/settings.ts, package.json,
# setup-preset.json) have no template counterpart there and are never
# compared, so they need no allowlist entry.

# .zfb/ directory is gitignored; doc-history-meta.json is written at build
# time by the doc-history plugin. It does not exist in the working tree.
.zfb/doc-history-meta.json

# scripts/run-b4push.sh is intentionally customized for this consuming site
# (full 9-step gate: format:md:check + template-drift + pin-parity +
# wrangler-pin + check + build + html + links + z-index; replaces the
# 4-step template default of check/build/html/manual-smoke).
scripts/run-b4push.sh

# pages/lib/_chrome.ts — site-specific MDX `mdxExtras` added. This site's docs
# corpus uses a custom <Playground> tag (the design-token-lint live browser
# demo, S4/#115); _chrome.ts imports PlaygroundIsland from ./_playground and
# registers it in the mdxExtras bag passed to createChrome(...) so MDX content
# resolves the tag through the host chrome instead of 500ing. Intentional
# divergence from the base template's empty mdxExtras block.
pages/lib/_chrome.ts

# pages/lib/_body-end-islands.tsx — @slot markers resolved; dynamicPageTransition
# wiring added. The base template ships @slot:body-end-islands:imports /
# :display-names / :extra-islands injection markers. Production has these
# slots resolved (removed) and the real dynamicPageTransition feature wiring
# inlined in their place: ClientRouterBootstrap (SPA transition bootstrap,
# hydrated via <Island when="load">) + PageLoadingOverlay (pure-SSR loading
# overlay), gated behind `settings.dynamicPageTransition` (true for this site —
# see epic #111 "Added: dynamicPageTransition").
pages/lib/_body-end-islands.tsx

# src/config/settings-types.ts — @slot:settings-types:trigger-names markers
# removed. The base template ships @slot: markers so compose can inject
# feature-specific trigger name types. Production has these slots resolved
# and removed.
src/config/settings-types.ts

# src/styles/global.css — @slot markers resolved; Futura brand typography +
# dynamicPageTransition/doc-history CSS added.
# The base template ships @slot:global-css:imports, :theme-tokens, and
# :feature-styles injection markers. Production has these slots resolved
# (removed) and adds:
#   - `@import "@takazudo/zudo-doc/page-loading.css"` + the
#     `--color-page-loading-overlay` token (dynamicPageTransition feature).
#   - the `--font-futura` token + `--zdc-doc-title-font` /
#     `--zdc-doc-title-weight` component-token overrides (rebrand every
#     framework-owned page-title h1 to Futura at normal weight, no-eject —
#     see epic #111 risk 4) and the `[data-header-logo]` rule (Futura on the
#     header site-name anchor, which exposes no className hook).
#   - the doc-history side-by-side diff viewer CSS (docHistory: true).
# The hand-written view-transition chrome-extraction block from the old model
# was deliberately NOT ported here — dynamicPageTransition's own
# `@takazudo/zudo-doc/features.css` is now the single driver, avoiding a
# double-drive of the same ::view-transition-* rules (epic #111 risk 5).
src/styles/global.css

# Feature shims vs. base W6A stubs — the base template ships no-op W6A stubs
# for these three components (so imports resolve at typecheck on a stub-only
# scaffold). This site enables the imageEnlarge / docHistory / sidebarToggle
# features, so each file is the feature-template re-export shim that forwards
# to the package island (@takazudo/zudo-doc/{image-enlarge,doc-history,
# desktop-sidebar-toggle-island}). The drift check's base-template pass always
# flags these shims because they differ from the base stubs; keep them
# allowlisted. (The feature-template pass would match the shims exactly, but a
# path-based allowlist entry skips both passes.)
src/components/desktop-sidebar-toggle.tsx
src/components/doc-history.tsx
src/components/image-enlarge.tsx

# src/integrations/claude-resources/* — MISSING (intentional).
# The claudeResources feature template ships an Astro-integration-style
# generator (src/integrations/claude-resources/{generate,escape-for-mdx}.ts +
# tests). This site instead drives claude-resources generation purely through
# the thin preset: `settings.claudeResources = { claudeDir: "../.claude",
# projectRoot: ".", scanRoot: ".." }` passed into `zudoDocPreset(...)` in
# zfb.config.ts (see src/config/settings.ts). No host-side integration files
# are needed — the package-owned preset plugin does the generation, anchoring
# generated `claude*` pages under doc/src/content/docs/ while scanning the
# repo-root .claude/ one level above doc/ (the hybrid-repo path, epic #111
# risk 2). Intentionally absent.
src/integrations/claude-resources/__tests__/escape-for-mdx.test.ts
src/integrations/claude-resources/__tests__/generate.test.ts
src/integrations/claude-resources/escape-for-mdx.ts
src/integrations/claude-resources/generate.ts

# tagGovernance — tags-audit.ts and tags-suggest.ts scripts are present in the
# tagGovernance feature template but have not been scaffolded for this site
